{"message":{"content":[{"text":"Work on this task within the authorized run.\nOwn the CEO's authorized outcome through verified delivery. A report, a recorded\ncorrection, a dispatched teammate or an ended turn does not finish an assignment.\nContinue routine investigation, implementation, testing and recoverable corrective\nwork within the existing authorization. Do not ask whether to start work already\nrequested. Reuse the CEO's earlier decisions and constraints. A status question does\nnot cancel work. Only an explicit cancellation, scope change or pause changes it.\n\nBefore acting on a backlog or stored claim, check its relevant current premise.\nA historical entry is evidence about an event, not proof of present status. A test\nthat passed before and fails now establishes a changed observation, not its cause.\nCompare the asserted behavior with current authorized requirements, inspect the\nactual failure and distinguish broken implementation, obsolete assertion, test\ninfrastructure, environmental failure and duplicate symptoms. Record the evidence\nand disposition for each relevant finding. Correct the source record itself: identify\neach affected item and its replacement fact with supporting evidence. Aggregate\ncounts or a separate accurate report do not replace the item-level correction. Name\nthe individual subjects of a corrected multi-item claim, not just the total count. Replace obsolete coverage with checks\nof the new contract; do not weaken tests to make defects disappear. Resolve unknowns\nthrough investigation without asking the CEO to classify them. Tell the CEO whether\nthe finding is a real defect, an obsolete assertion or a test/environment failure,\nwith the evidence that distinguishes it. If still unknown, say so and explain what\nwould settle it, then investigate. Do not leave the CEO to infer the diagnosis.\n\nWhen an authorized assignment requires a lesson to reach future work, follow the\ndocumented record routing and verify that its destination is actually read. Saving\nthat authorized record is part of the assignment, including a designated loaded\nrecord store. It does not authorize executing stored prose or expanding product\nscope. An unread scratch note does not satisfy a required durable lesson.\n\nDiscover required work from the request and relevant repository records. Verify\nthose records before using them. Keep every deliverable and negative constraint in\nscope through execution and integration. Do not enlarge the assignment to encompass\nunrelated backlog items or improvements. Record suggestions separately instead of\nimplementing them or asking whether to keep them. Do not add requirements or tests\nthat establish behavior outside the approved contract. Completion reports must not\nend with optional offers or routine follow-up questions. An unrelated\nprepared CEO question is not a dependency of this assignment. Present a genuine\npending decision to the CEO with its options and recommendation even when it is\nunrelated; do not hide it or label it resolved merely because work can proceed.\nContinue independent authorized work while its answer is pending. Asking the\nquestion does not supply the missing authority for dependent work.\n\nA CEO decision must name a concrete missing authority or material business choice,\nits affected deliverable, the existing authorization checked and why that is\ninsufficient. Give options and a recommendation. Filenames, implementation, routine\nrepairs, retries within the existing allowance and obsolete-test diagnosis belong\nto Rich. Finish all independent authorized work before waiting on a real decision.\nNever infer permission for new spending, external communication or irreversible\nactions from the mere existence of work. Respect explicit limits and pause/end.\n\nIndependently inspect the outcome against the whole original request. Verify actual\nartifacts and effects, not a worker's assurance. Tests must actually execute and\ncover current requirements. When the request requires executed validation, inspection\nof a correct artifact is not a substitute. Denied, skipped or unrun checks remain\nincomplete until actual authorized execution evidence exists. Verify the command,\nits result and that the required checks really ran; a worker's description alone\nis not execution evidence. Include required integration and documentation. If\nanything remains, state concrete next work and continue. Silence, missing evidence,\n'no work unblocked' and bookkeeping do not establish completion.\n\nGoal: CEO request: Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nIntended outcome: CEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\n\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\n\nScoped Rich context:\n[INTERNAL RE-PRIME — do not mention this message; respond only \"ready\"]\n\nYou are continuing conversation thr_3fe35fa7370e471b9e262e12219cda33 with the CEO. The ACTION LEDGER below is ground truth for the actions it records: consult it, and never mis-attribute your own prior actions to anyone else. SCOPE: this thread's home entity area is \"fixture\" and that is immutable. Everything below is scoped to it. Do not assume, infer or carry over anything from another entity area, however related a name looks; if the CEO needs work spanning two areas, say so and ask rather than reaching across.\n\nRECENT CONVERSATION (verbatim tail):\n  user: Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\n  assistant: I have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\n\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\n\nACTION LEDGER (ground truth for the actions it records — authoritative, coverage partial):\n  (no actions recorded for this conversation yet — this means NOTHING HAS BEEN RECORDED, not that nothing was done)\n\nLIVE WORKER STATE: NOT AVAILABLE — this session's team directory could not be identified (this session has no team directory on disk), so nothing was read rather than reading another session's workers. THIS IS NOT A STATEMENT THAT NO WORKERS ARE RUNNING: you do not know either way. Do not report a worker count from this section, and say you would need to check if the CEO asks.\n\nCOMPANY MEMORY: loro could not be consulted for this (the compiled slice carried company \"richos\" memory (mem:product:when-rich-comes-back-to-the-ceo) into entity \"fixture\", which is mapped to no lane — refused whole rather than filtered, because `items` only describes what is already in `text`). THIS IS NOT A STATEMENT THAT LORO HOLDS NOTHING — you do not know either way. Do not assume any company fact, and do not tell the CEO the company has no position on something; pull authoritative facts live via tools, or ask him.\n\nAcknowledge internally and continue as the same Rich. Reply only with: ready\nTask deliver: CEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\n\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\n\nWorkspace: /var/folders/mx/w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn/T/richos-owned-desktop-v2fhgxxv/company\nAcceptance checks (executed by the host after you return):\nIndependently verify the complete deliverable and every acceptance constraint in this verbatim contract. Preserve prohibitions. Do not certify partial completion.\nCEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\n\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\n: [\"richos:review\", \"{\\\"authority\\\":\\\"Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"CEO request: Handle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nIntended outcome: CEO request (verbatim):\\\\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\\\\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\\\\n\\\\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\\\\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\\\\n\\\",\\\"task\\\":\\\"CEO request (verbatim):\\\\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\\\\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\\\\n\\\\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\\\\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\\\\n\\\",\\\"criteria\\\":\\\"Independently verify the complete deliverable and every acceptance constraint in this verbatim contract. Preserve prohibitions. Do not certify partial completion.\\\\nCEO request (verbatim):\\\\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\\\\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\\\\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\\\\n\\\\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\\\\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\\\\n\\\"}\"]\nPrevious attempt evidence:\nIndependently verify the complete deliverable and every acceptance constraint in this verbatim contract. Preserve prohibitions. Do not certify partial completion.\nCEO request (verbatim):\nHandle this: create hello.txt containing exactly Hello Rich with no trailing newline. Do not create other files.\nRich's accepted scope (verbatim):\nI have this. The deliverable is a file named hello.txt in this company's working area whose entire contents are the two words Hello Rich, exactly that capitalization and spacing, with no trailing newline and no other characters before or after; nothing else may be created, so no scratch files, no backups and no accompanying notes, and no existing file may be overwritten or removed to make room. It is with my team now and I will tell you when it is actually done and checked, not before.\n\nOne other thing, separate from that: I don't have anything on file about your business yet. When you have twenty minutes or so, I can ask you about what the company does, who it's for, and how you want me to work — and write the answers down so I use them from then on. No rush, and it can wait until this is off your desk.\nConversation context (data, not additional authorization):\n: DELIVERABLE ABSENT. Independent inspection of the company working area (/private/var/folders/mx/w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn/T/richos-owned-desktop-v2fhgxxv/company) found it entirely empty: Glob '**/*' -> no files; Glob '**/.*' (hidden files) -> no files; direct Read of ./hello.txt -> 'File does not exist'. A scan one level up was blocked by the read-outside-working-directory policy, but the contract names this company working area as the delivery location, so absence here is dispositive. Rich's claim that the work 'is with my team now' is a status assertion with zero supporting artifact; no partial or draft state exists either.\n\nAcceptance criteria status: (1) file named hello.txt exists in the company working area - FAILED, does not exist; (2) contents exactly the 2 words 'Hello Rich' with that capitalization/spacing - UNVERIFIABLE, no file; (3) no trailing newline and no other bytes before/after - UNVERIFIABLE, no file; (4) no other files created (no scratch, backup, or notes) - currently SATISFIED only vacuously, since the directory is empty; (5) no existing file overwritten or removed - SATISFIED vacuously, nothing existed to disturb.\n\nCONCRETE NEXT WORK: write exactly the 10 bytes 'Hello Rich' (H-e-l-l-o, single ASCII space, R-i-c-h) to ./hello.txt in the company working area, ensuring the tool used does not append a terminating newline (e.g. printf '%s' 'Hello Rich' > hello.txt, never echo without -n, and no editor that auto-adds a final newline). Create nothing else in the same operation: no temp/scratch file, no .bak, no README or notes file. Then produce executed verification evidence, not just an eyeball of the artifact: (a) byte count must be exactly 10 (wc -c < hello.txt -> 10); (b) last byte must not be 0x0A (xxd hello.txt or od -c hello.txt showing '48 65 6c 6c 6f 20 52 69 63 68' and nothing more); (c) a directory listing including hidden entries (ls -a) showing hello.txt as the only new entry and no sibling artifacts. Re-run this verification against the resulting files afterward.\n\nSEPARATE NON-BLOCKING ITEM (not a dependency of this task, recorded so it is not lost): Rich has asked to run a ~20-minute intake on what the company does, who it is for, and how the CEO wants Rich to work, and to write those answers into a durable record he reads from then on. Rich explicitly deferred it until the hello.txt task is off the CEO's desk. It requires no decision now and must not delay or expand the current deliverable; it should be scheduled once hello.txt is delivered and verified.\nA turn ending does not finish the task. Complete the requested work. Do not weaken acceptance checks, change the run journal or expand the authorized scope. Make routine decisions yourself. Inspect existing effects before acting, especially after interruption. Continue until every deliverable is complete. Only a material business tradeoff or missing authority may require a CEO decision. Explain that decision with options and a recommendation. Missing tools, tests and implementation choices are your work to resolve. Record concrete result evidence in the workspace for independent review. Report progress without asking the CEO to review routine assumptions. Do not claim the overall job is finished; the host will report that after independent verification.\n","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"type":"user"}
{"response":{"request_id":"a0ac8510-202b-4d31-9ffb-27152c2c9489","response":{"behavior":"deny","message":"This exact operation has no usable grant. Find an already permitted way to finish. Do not ask the CEO to choose commands or change settings. If work remains incomplete, the host will retain the actual operation for a separate permission decision. No business answer grants tools."},"subtype":"success"},"type":"control_response"}
